restoreBackup — which replaces 8 config tables — logs: `s.recordOp(c, "restore", "backup", fmt.Sprintf("backup#%d", req.ID), nil, nil)` (backup.go:85); for the arbitrary-content path req.ID==0, so the only trace is the literal string 'backup#0' with empty before/after (see authz-2). rollbackConfig logs only `gin.H{"rolled_back_to": v}` with before=nil (configstatus.go:58). batchKeywords replace-mode wipes the whole keyword library first — guard.go:112-113 `if req.Mode == "replace" {
		s.db.Where("1 = 1").Delete(&model.GuardKeyword{})` — yet logs only the created count with before=nil (guard.go:125). updateModel records `nil` as before (models.go:169). Login events: unknown username returns before any recordOp (auth.go:34-36 `if err := s.db.Where("username = ?", req.Username).First(&u).Error; err != nil {
	s.fail(c, http.StatusUnauthorized, 40102, "用户名或密码错误")
		return`), wrong password likewise (auth.go:76-79), so brute force leaves zero audit rows; successful login logs with operatorOf(c)=="anonymous" because AuthMiddleware never ran (auth.go:132 `s.recordOp(c, "login", "auth", u.Username, nil, nil)` + server.go:99-106 default), and logout mislabels its action as "login" (auth.go:153). Finally, GET reads of the most sensitive bulk data are not recorded at all: downloadBackup (backup.go:45-54), exportConfig (configstatus.go:62-71), exportCallLogs/exportOpLogs (audit.go:95-110, 173-186), callLogDetail full input/output text (audit.go:81-82).

The audit rows embed a fully caller-controlled string: gateway.go:334 `ap.alias = cr.Model` is set from the parsed request body BEFORE alias resolution, and failed lookups are still persisted because errors bypass sampling (gateway.go:253-258 shouldAuditCall: `if status != "ok" {
		return true
	}`, write at 315-317; the 404 path stores it: gateway.go:357 `ap.errMsg = "unknown model alias: " + cr.Model`). exportCallLogs then writes it raw: audit.go:102-105 `w.Write([]string{r.RequestID, ..., r.ModelAlias, upstreamLabel(...),` / `..., strconv.FormatBool(r.Blocked), r.BlockReason})` — no leading-quote/`=`/`+`/`-`/`@` filtering (csv.Writer quotes for parsing safety but does nothing about spreadsheet formula semantics). The same applies to error_msg-derived columns and to exportOpLogs' target/before/after (audit.go:179-181).

